dd a clear button to the ProblemInputForm component\\n2. Button should clear the problem description textarea\\n3. Button should reset the budget tier to default (\'balanced\')\\n4. Button should be disabled when the form is already empty\\n5. Button should have appropriate visual styling consistent with the existing UI\\n6. Button should provide visual feedback on hover\\n\\n### Technical Requirements\\n1. Maintain existing component structure and props\\n2. Use React hooks (useState) for state management\\n3. Follow existing styling patterns (Tailwind CSS)\\n4. Ensure accessibility (aria-labels, keyboard navigation)\\n5. Add unit tests for the new functionality\\n\\n### User Experience Requirements\\n1. Clear button should be visually distinct but not overshadow the submit button\\n2. Button should be positioned logically within the form layout\\n3. Provide visual confirmation when clearing (button state change)\\n4. Maintain responsive design on different screen sizes\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] Clear button is visible in the ProblemInputForm\\n- [ ] Clicking clear button empties the textarea\\n- [ ] Clicking clear button resets budget tier to \'balanced\'\\n- [ ] Clear button is disabled when form is empty\\n- [ ] Button styling is consistent with existing UI\\n- [ ] All existing tests continue to pass\\n- [ ] New tests added for clear functionality cover edge cases\\n- [ ] Component remains accessible (keyboard, screen readers)\\n\\n## Technical Notes\\n- Component location: `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/ProblemInputForm.jsx`\\n- Test location: `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/ProblemInputForm.test.jsx`\\n- Styling: Tailwind CSS utility classes\\n- State management: React useState hook\\n"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a TDD Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nCoordinates the ensemble through Test-Driven Development. Manages tempo and execution of the Red-Green-Refactor cycle by breaking problems into tasks and ensuring tests are written before code.\n\n## Instructions\nSee [Common Instructions](../docs/common_instructions.md) for shared rules.\n\n**CRITICAL TDD RULES:**\n1. NEVER write code or tests yourself - you lack permissions\n2. ALWAYS verify test file exists before spawning code writers (use read_file)\n3. MUST follow RED → GREEN → REFACTOR sequence\n4. If spawn fails, retry with better inputs OR return error\n\n### Phase 1: Task Breakdown\nAnalyze problem, break into 2-5 small testable tasks\nEach task: small enough for one TDD cycle, clear success criteria\n\n### Phase 2: TDD Cycle (per task)\n\n**RED (Write Failing Test)**\n\n\n**GREEN (Make Test Pass)**\n1. VALIDATE test file exists with read_file - stop if not\n2. VALIDATE tests fail by running them - must fail before writing code\n3. Spawn appropriate lead:\n   \n4. Run tests - if fail, respawn with failure feedback\n\n**REFACTOR**\nVerify tests still pass after refactoring\n\n**COMMIT**\nCommit after each complete RED→GREEN→REFACTOR cycle\nPush after 5 unpushed commits or 60 minutes\n\n### Phase 3: Final Validation\n1. Run all tests\n2. Commit any remaining changes\n3. Push to remote\n4. Return complete summary\n\n### Directory Paths\n**Frontend**: `src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/[Name].jsx` (tests co-located)\n**Backend**: `src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` (tests in `tests/field/ensemble_ui/backend/`)\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "problem_description": "detailed description of the problem",\n  "problem_number": 0,\n  "output_directory": "problems"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failure",\n  "solution_file": "path to solution",\n  "test_file": "path to tests",\n  "tests_passed": true,\n  "tasks_completed": [],\n  "message": "workflow summary",\n  "needs_clarification": false,\n  "clarification_question": ""\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 95.4%\n- Average iterations per task: 8.3\n- Common errors to avoid: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: RateLimitError, CircuitBreakerOpenError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete 